## Commits

Follow the commit-message convention used by the project. If none is established, [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) is a common option:

```text
type(scope): concise summary
```

Keep each commit focused. Explain motivation or consequences in the body when the subject is not enough.

## Pull requests

Follow the project's branch and review process. A useful pull request describes the problem, the change, and how it was verified. Update relevant documentation and call out compatibility changes or unresolved risks.

## Releases

Follow the project's versioning and release process. If the project maintains a changelog, record notable user-facing changes there.{% if references.security %}

## Security issues

Report vulnerabilities privately using [the security policy]({{ references.security }}). Do not post sensitive details in a public issue.{% endif %}
